+# CIA and FAA/NORAD/Mineta: independent verification and integration
+
+October26,2026 (America/New_York). **15 qualified records: CC001–CC003 and FA001–FA012.** The CIA continuation was already public; these three records give it master IDs without counting CL001–CL008 again. The twelve FAA records include adverse findings, contrary evidence, source limitations and a failure of our own audio method. They are not15 independent suspicious events or proof of a conspiracy.
+
+The strongest affirmative accountability record in this bounded check is the DOT review’s finding that three executives learned a liaison-timing answer was inaccurate and did not correct it with the Commission. That is distinct from the same review’s finding of insufficient evidence of knowing falsity about hijack notifications. Preserve both findings. No attack-purpose, WTC7 access, demolition, fabricated al-Qaeda attribution or coordinated-concealment finding is established by these records.
+
+## What was done and what changed
+
+- Re-read the two CIA review pages, the relevant hearing exchanges, selected Staff17/Commission notes and finding-aid pages, the relevant DOT main-body and facsimile passages, and the tape-release index/letter. Six public source acquisitions succeeded; hearing/Staff17/finding-aid/tape-letter hashes match held copies.
+- Acquired the official30-page DOT report directly after the sender’s earlier403. Both access outcomes remain in the record. Official/report-packet hashes differ; OCR similarity is a locator aid and is not semantic or byte authentication.
+- Direct CIA URL still returned HTML, not PDF. The mirror’s provenance limitation remains; search-index text does not close it.
+- Independently checked all-zero control PCM, saved ASR output hashes/repetition/overrun counts and stated-time/page arithmetic. No audio was uploaded or ASR rerun; no spoken words or clock anchors were accepted.
+- Performed eight bounded public queries for originals/dispositions; did not recover the native message, PEOC alarm/log or final personnel-action packages. Their exact next targets stay open.
+
+[Source URLs/hashes](SOURCES.json) · [complete selected passages/field transcriptions](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md) · [exact line pins](EXCERPT-PINS.json) · [all findings](findings.json) · [open originals](OPEN-QUESTIONS.json) · [search coverage](SEARCH-LOG.json) · [independent audio check](AUDIO-CONTROL-CHECK.json) · [requirements](CHECKLIST.md).
+
+## Reading and inference discipline
+
+Physical PDF page numbers are one-based. CIA physical92–93 are printed67–68; Commission notes physical16 is printed464. Staff17’s physical and printed numbers coincide in the inspected pages. The official DOT report’s main body is physical/printed1–13, while the release packet inserts/reorders front matter and appends facsimiles; use exact page pins rather than assuming a universal offset. G paragraph labels are this review’s derivative, not the sender’s P labels. Source extractions retain errors; table paraphrases are expressly marked and visually checked.
+
+We read the complete extracted passages used below and16 selected rendered pages. This is not a whole-source visual authentication of491CIA pages,429release pages,145finding-aid pages or the source recordings. The final report’s source notes were inspected, not every underlying note/log or the entire final-report body. Multiple Commission publication forms are not independent clock measurements. All original conflicting accounts and the prior editions remain intact.
+
+<a id="cc001"></a>
+## CC001 / M161 — Later access to the notification-claim cable is reported; reliance remains inferred
+
+**Type:** Review-reported access plus explicitly conditional inference.
+
+CIA OIG printed67 / physical92 reports July2,2001 access to SCALEC134684 dated January5,2000, before the July13 revisit recommendation, and a July23 follow-up. The cable asserted that travel documents had reached the FBI.
+
+- The review explicitly says the reason for the early access is unclear and treats the reader’s likely belief that the FBI already knew as an inference. No native audit, cable, recipient receipt or contemporaneous reader explanation was acquired.
+- The January5,2001 identification-cable quotation elsewhere on the same page and January5,2000 SCALEC134684 reference are different source descriptions; neither is silently changed.
+- M154 already records the unconfirmed notification assertion. This entry adds the later-access/reliance question, not a second independent proof of delivery failure or deliberate misinformation.
+
+**Exact source/derivative locations:** [CIA05-P092](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#cia05-p092) lines5–69; [CIA05-P093](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#cia05-p093) lines70–140. Full source URLs and SHA-256 values are in EXCERPT-PINS.json.
+
+**What would test/change this:** Join native access/print history and the exact cable to July tasking/follow-up, recipient-side incoming records and the August23 message; distinguish genuine informal delivery, mistaken reliance and deliberate misleading documentation.
+
+<a id="cc002"></a>
+## CC002 / M162 — Possible paper-copy use limits an inference from electronic audit silence
+
+**Type:** Review-reported countercheck and unresolved medium/identity join.
+
+CIA OIG printed68 / physical93 footnote23 reports an officer’s account of basing a CIR on a March5 cable despite no electronic access record, and discusses a possible hard copy supplied by someone else.
+
+- The review reports only the former DCOS accessed and printed that cable at the Station between June2000 and August24,2001. This does not prove actual paper delivery to that officer.
+- The body separately describes a March6 cable opened August21. Preserve March5 in footnote23 and March6 in the body as distinct references; identity to one underlying cable has not been proved.
+- Electronic audit silence alone cannot conclusively exclude paper use. Conversely, a possible paper route cannot establish successful FBI receipt of the different January notification claim. Competing-priority statements and August23 dissemination remain in the record.
+
+**Exact source/derivative locations:** [CIA05-P093](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#cia05-p093) lines70–140. Full source URLs and SHA-256 values are in EXCERPT-PINS.json.
+
+**What would test/change this:** Acquire exact March5/March6 cable identifiers, CIR source notes, printer records and any paper routing/receipt; compare separately with the January delivery claim.
+
+<a id="cc003"></a>
+## CC003 / M163 — Dated NARA folder identifiers narrow original-record searches without supplying the originals
+
+**Type:** Archival locator finding; not missingness-to-destruction evidence.
+
+The January14,2009 finding aid identifies Team1 boxes18–19 and23–27, Daniel Marcus boxes1–3, and Team1A box39 as specific routes for CIA briefings, responses, document requests and access records.
+
+- Team1 box18 CIA index and May20,2003 DCI briefing are annotated withdrawal-notice-only; box19 Document Requests–DCI15–45 has no such title annotation. Box26 marks DCI#6 only in the listed request group; do not apply that qualifier to every request.
+- Box25 titles include Late2003Memo to CIA and CIA Responses; CIA Briefing–7/11/03 on Info Sharing with FBI; OctoberMemo to CIA and CIA Response. Counsel files include agency certifications, CIA(3folders) and DocumentRequests. Team1A box39 separately lists DocumentAccess–FBI and withdrawal-only DCIRequest#4ThirdSupplementNotes.
+- The aid is a dated inventory, not a current release census or proof that the target original messages are in those folders. No folder payloads, current withdrawal decisions or native CIA package were acquired.
+
+**Exact source/derivative locations:** [NARA-AID-P006](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p006) lines1164–1216; [NARA-AID-P007](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p007) lines1217–1270; [NARA-AID-P027](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p027) lines1271–1323; [NARA-AID-P029](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p029) lines1324–1378; [NARA-AID-P030](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p030) lines1379–1432; [NARA-AID-P043](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#nara-aid-p043) lines1433–1485. Full source URLs and SHA-256 values are in EXCERPT-PINS.json.
+
+**What would test/change this:** Locate exact folder/withdrawal notices and their current release history, then test the native-message/routing questions. No outreach or fees authorized.
+
+<a id="fa001"></a>
+## FA001 / M164 — Official notification accounts differ in flight identity as well as stated times
+
+**Type:** Conflicting published official accounts.
+
+The reproduced September18,2001 NORAD release and FAA table give AA77 notification09:24 and UA93N/A or NA. May23,2003 testimony gives UA93 possible-hijack notice09:16. The 2004 Commission account gives first NEADS UA93 notice10:07, AA77 missing09:34, and identifies the09:24 log entry as phantom AA11.
+
+- Preserve all versions. The shift09:16 to10:07 is51 minutes of stated anchors, not a calibrated operational delay or measured clock offset. A missing-aircraft notice, hijack notice and inferred flight identity are different events.
+- The 2001 NORAD release also gives UA17508:43 and estimated crashes09:37/10:03 for AA77/UA93; the FAA table gives UA17509:05 and09:38/10:04 crashes. These facsimile values are retained without normalization.
+- No independent reconstruction of native radar, phone recordings, log entries or clocks was performed. The Commission’s correction claim is itself preserved as a source position, not selected as controlling by this audit.
+
+**Exact source/derivative locations:** [DOT-RELEASE-P091](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#dot-release-p091) lines738–743; [DOT-RELEASE-P105](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#dot-release-p105) lines744–749; [H03-G153](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#h03-g153) lines1852–1857; [H03-G154](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#h03-g154) lines1858–1863; [STAFF17-P017](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#staff17-p017) lines809–845; [STAFF17-P018](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#staff17-p018) lines846–882; [STAFF17-P019](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#staff17-p019) lines883–925; [H04-G206](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#h04-g206) lines1888–1893; [H04-G207](SOURCE-EXCERPTS.md#h04-g207) lines1894–1899. Full source URLs and SHA-256 values are in EXCERPT-PINS.json.
+
+**What would test/change this:** Obtain original NEADS logs/tapes and FAA notice chains with channel provenance and at least two independent clock anchors; retain event types and version dates.
+
+<a id="fa002"></a>
+## FA002 / M165 — DOT found insufficient evidence of knowing falsity yet called the UA93 omission explanation unreasonable
+
+**Type:** Issue-specific oversight assessment and counterevidence.
+
